[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'What would your ideal sales rep do all day? This is Signal, our sales agent built on HyperAgent. Signal works 24/7 finding new leads, building personalized landing pages for every prospect, responding to inbound, nurturing, following up, and then tracking'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything perfectly in CRM. And it learns from every single interaction, so it gets better with each run. Signal is a free agent template on HyperAgent Marketplace. You can grab it at the link in the description. Let\'s dive in. So, I asked Signal to make a little explainer'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about itself. &gt;&gt; Nice. &gt;&gt; So, this is how Signal works. Every single run it\'s going through live mode, and it\'s going to work on some outbound. So, it\'s going to discover new prospects for the company. It\'s going to enrich'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'them using data from Apollo. It builds every single one of them a personalized landing page, and it it will even put a video or other assets on that landing page specific to that person. It builds out this command center that holds'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything together. It will write drafts directly in Gmail. While it\'s in Gmail, runs its inbound loop. So, it will check that inbox for anything that came in since the last run. It will triage them, qualify leads. If it\'s like'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a perfect warm lead, it will just go ahead and offer the booking link to that person. If it needs a little bit more back and forth or qualification, it will do that. It will nurture cold leads as well. It has some guardrails on how to do that. And then the key idea here is'

[01:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that it\'s always on. It can just keep running, keep observing, keep learning, and getting better. &gt;&gt; Tell me about how it keeps getting better. &gt;&gt; So, looking at Signal\'s profile here on the HyperAgent web app, we can see that self-learning is on. And so, it has many'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different ways to uh register its learnings. The simplest is, of course, by storing memories. And so, it will just store these kind of like sticky notes of different things that it has learned, different preferences, maybe'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'messaging that has worked, facts about different buyers or different types of buyers. It can also make more kind of lasting updates to its skills or even its own system prompt. If it\'s things that uh are kind of a little bit more'

[01:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fundamental, and then it wants to keep applying for every future action. &gt;&gt; Amazing. &gt;&gt; Yeah. &gt;&gt; Skills are like a big part of how an agent runs things repeatedly and predictably in a way that we want to see in either inbox or how it triages and'

[02:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'categorizes leads. So, what are the skills that you gave Signal to make sure that it is working in the way that we like in our process? &gt;&gt; Yeah, so it starts with some out-of-the-box skills around things like creating those outbound assets for every'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'single buyer, skills around how to enrich data with Apollo, skills to do with updating its CRM and running that nurture campaign. It also benefits from all the built-in global skills that we have in Hyper Agent. And so, it can keep'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'updating that playbook and it will start making those more specific to your company the more you use it. &gt;&gt; Nice. &gt;&gt; So, I ran Signal for this company called Swish Solar. It\'s this really cool company that\'s making solar panel self-cleaning technology. I'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gave Signal basically just their website, just their URL, and said, "Go into your sales loop for this company." And after a few runs, this was what it came back with. So, this is the command'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'center that it has built for all of the outbound, all of the inbound that it\'s running. And so, you can see each of these cards right here. This is a basically qualified buyer based on the deep research that Signal did that is an'

